From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:22:25 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: clpc: raise DRAM and fabric floors for ANE work

On the Neo (T8140) nothing raises the memory controller (DCS) or the SoC
fabric while the Neural Engine runs: the CLPC only follows CPU and GPU
load. A MobileNetV1 EXECUTE then takes 2.3-2.5 ms. With DCS 4 and fabric
3, the floor the GPU already gets for streaming work, it takes
1.25-1.31 ms; the engine time drops from 1.8-2.0 ms to about 1.0 ms.

Add an ANE input next to the host GPU one. A driver gets a client with
apple_clpc_ane_get() and reports work in flight with
apple_clpc_ane_set_active(). The client has its own reference, so a late
publication or put after the CLPC went away is harmless, and getting it
never defers: without a bound CLPC the ANE runs without the floor. An
idle-to-active edge samples at once, a request shorter than the sampling
period is latched until the next sample, and the per-SoC ANE rail states
then merge with the CPU and GPU demand under the usual hold.

T8140 asks for DCS 4 and fabric 3. Other SoCs have no ANE input. A
root-only debugfs file, ane_states, overrides the two states (clamped
to each rail) for measurements, and the status file reports the ANE
input and reason bit 32.

KUnit covers demand and hold, short requests, provider removal, cold
wake, a missing provider and the state overrides.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 7801f81ca057673162aefad164fea6fc8af2d512)
[j604: clpc.c context: this base has no gpu_input field and prints gpu read errors in the status line; only the ANE field, its doc line and the ANE status block are added]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
